facebook apple amazon netflix and google  these five companies have a reputation  for paying some of the most exorbitant  salaries and offering the best perks in  the world at least tech workers  google for example has a median salary  of 295 000 per year while facebook comes  in at 292 000 per year and that's just  the median if you have any sort of  seniority within these companies they'll  be making closer to 500 000 per year if  not more  20 years ago these types of salaries  were only offered to c-suite executives  but these tech companies have made them  more common than ever  aside from these insane pay packages  many tech companies also have generous  work from home policies and unlimited  vacation time considering these  extraordinary perks working at these  companies is the top career goal for  many and getting a job at one of these  companies is extremely difficult at  google for instance the chances of  scoring a job for the average applicant  is just 0.2 percent hearing this you  would think that the people who make it  to the other side would be extremely  loyal and stick around for decades  but this is actually not the case  in fact these companies not only rank at  the top of the salary lists but also at  the top of the turnover lists  the average tenure of employees at these  companies is usually no more than two  years now it should be noted that this  study measures tenure and a non-turnover  so it is a bit skewed these companies  are always hiring new employees and  growing their workforces so naturally  the average tenure is going to skew  towards zero with that being said though  it's no secret that these companies have  high turnover if you know people within  these companies you know that most of  them jump around every few years and  this is the same case with most of their  co-workers as well  not to mention the thousands of youtube  videos and reddit posts about quitting  fame so why in the world do the best  places to work also have the highest  turnover  one of the top reasons many thank  engineers aren't enticed to stay at  their jobs is because the salary isn't  that big of a deal for them this isn't  to say that they're ungrateful for their  opportunities or that they don't care  about money when they enter the industry  they probably very much cared about the  high compensation and cool perks however  by the time they're 10 years into the  industry most of them simply achieve  financial freedom now they don't become  sent to millionaires or billionaires but  they almost always become  multi-millionaires if not decca  millionaires  but wait a minute even if you're getting  paid to 300 dollars per year  this only comes out to three million  dollars within 10 years  and by the time you deal with  california's taxes and living expenses  you'd be lucky to be left with a million  dollars so how did these guys manage to  save up over 5 million or 10 million  well the answer lies in stock  compensation every entry-level software  engineer at facebook earns 42 000 worth  of stock compensation every single year  you just have to get promoted once for  this number to nearly double to eighty  one thousand dollars per year and by the  time you get your second or third  promotion your stock compensation itself  is worth six figures if not multiple six  figures  also it's not like this money is being  invested into a 401k or the s p 500 this  money is literally being invested into  the fastest growing companies in the  world  over the past 10 years facebook grew 21x  amazon and group 21x apple group 13x  netflix crew 90x and google group 10x  now let's say you ended up at the  slowest grower which is google in 2012  and that you decide to stick around for  10 years  maybe you start at the lowest level  which is level three and make it to  level five this would mean that your  average stock compensation during this  time period would be eighty three  thousand dollars per year we can even  estimate conservatively and call it  seventy thousand dollars per year we can  also say that you're a financial idiot  and that you live paycheck to paycheck  you don't contribute to your 401k and  that you have no savings as long as you  don't sell your stock compensation you  would enjoy an annual growth rate of  27.8 percent and you'd be left with a  2.6 million dollars by the end of 10  years and that's the worst case scenario  if you were to do the same thing in  netflix which was the fastest growing of  the bunch you'd enjoy an annual growth  rate of 61  which would leave you with 13.3 million  dollars  if you jumped around every couple of  years like most of these guys do it you  probably would have ended somewhere in  between those two numbers likely five to  ten million dollars and that's just  stock compensation if you take advantage  of this company's 401k plans and invest  in the s p 500 yourself you can easily  boost a net worth of over 10 million  dollars by the time you're in your mid  30s when you're in such a position  earning more money gives you basically  zero tangible value people who are still  pursuing vault after this point are  simply playing the money game and seeing  how high they can get  but in terms of daily life earning more  money gives them no additional value and  they can retire at any time so it's no  wonder why paying salaries are not  enough to retain these employees  as you can see the vast majority of fang  employees become financially free at a  very young age so they're not driven to  stay at a company just for the salary  but even if they were driven by just the  salary it would still be in their best  interest and not stay at the same  company here's the thing when you stay  at the same company at best you'll earn  a three to five percent raise every year  if you switch companies strategically  however you can squeeze in a 10 to 20  raise every couple of years  and when you do this for a prolonged  period of time the person who constantly  switched jobs ends up earning a lot more  than the loyal employee according to  forbes employees who stay at companies  for longer than two years are paid 50  less on average now this isn't to say  that you should switch companies every  24 months because that'll likely become  a red flag very quickly  but it is in your best interest to  switch periodically as in every five to  seven years and this is especially true  in the fang world while it's extremely  difficult to get into fang once you're  in and have a couple of years under your  build it's comically easy to switch  between these companies here's the thing  the reason acceptance rates at fan  companies are so low is not because  these companies don't need more talent  these companies are always desperate for  more talent and the reason acceptance  rates are so low is because it's  extremely difficult to find employees  that are on the caliber that they're  looking for but if you've already passed  the screening process of one of their  competitors they can be pretty confident  that you'll be a good hire  fan companies are infamous for  approaching employees from competitors  in fact they're almost always embroiled  in a bunch of lawsuits regarding  stealing employees and intellectual  property and things along those lines so  as top tier thank talent you can use  this rivalry amongst these companies to  maximize your own compensation something  else to note is that switching to other  fan companies is not their only option  in many cases they go on to found their  own companies and given that these guys  have intelligence experience and  networks the odds are very much stacked  in their favor this is why companies  like xiaomi pinterest ship technologies  upstart and youtube were all founded by  x silicon valley employees imagine if  eric yuan stayed at cisco instead of  founding zoom or if reed hoffman stayed  at paypal instead of founding linkedin  more times than not these guys have  their eyes on targets that are much  larger than just 10 to 15 million  dollars often times that they're looking  for hundreds of millions if not billions  so they're not gonna stick around at  google just so they can get a few  hundred thousand dollars and free food  and given that fang recruits the  absolute best talent in the world it's  not surprising that many of their  employees have such ambitions for most  of them it's just a matter of time until  they outgrow their roles and fame  while larger goals and financial freedom  often play a factor in fang employees  jumping ship these are not the only  reasons  often times it just comes down to  employees burning out and either wanting  to take it slow or get a fresh start we  commonly hear about how great it is to  work at these companies but a lot of  that is simply because that's how these  companies want us to perceive them all  of these companies are master marketers  when it comes to selling their products  and it's no different when it comes to  recruiting they want us to think that  their jobs are the absolute best when in  reality their jobs are actually super  stressful but wait a minute don't fan  companies have extremely generous  vacation policies and paid time off and  things like that well yes they do but  here's the cool thing for them these  companies don't have to be the bad guys  to cultivate an extremely competitive  and stressful working environment they  don't need to implement cutthroat  managers and directors or hang scary  deadlines over your head when you place  thousands of the smartest and the most  competitive individuals together it's  only natural that they're gonna try to  outdo each other you don't need to scare  them or threaten them to work hard and  not take vacations these guys are  naturally not going to take vacations  because they want to shine they want  that next promotion and they want that  higher status and they want to boost  their egos they all have their own  selfish reasons for working hard and  they're all highly motivated which works  out perfectly for these companies the  companies can be the good guys offering  great salaries and awesome perks while  the employees end up working 60 hours  per week or more by themselves many of  these guys thrive under these working  conditions and they end up as a vp at a  fan company or a c-suite executive at a  startup but many also burn themselves  out and end up scaling back or switching  companies this is why most employees at  apple report struggling with burnout and  why almost half of apple and amazon  employees don't have a close friend at  work this is also why only about half of  employees at most fan companies are  actually happy at their jobs the only  exception to this rule is netflix and  the reason they have such happy  employees is because they lean into a  contractor model that turns over  employees even faster so most of their  employees never even get past the  honeymoon phase personally i've seen  this play out in real life in high  school i had a computer science teacher  from fang and a coach that was from the  nfl while both of these guys were from  completely different industries i think  their reasoning for taking such a  massive pay cut were identical they were  simply burnt out from always having to  perform at their peak ability now i  should also mention that the computer  science teacher has since returned to  fang so clearly these guys can never  truly suppress their inner urge to  constantly progress in their careers  but at the same time they're never truly  satisfied at any one of these jobs  they're constantly in this limbo state  where they're hopping jobs every few  years perpetually trying to find inner  peace  in the end while fan companies love  trying to convince us that they're the  best places to work it's simply not true  job satisfaction is usually not derived  from high salaries or fancy perks  virtually all the jobs with the highest  satisfaction have something to do with  helping others whether that be providing  educational services or therapy and at  feng all you're usually doing is making  the biggest companies in the world even  bigger there's also the whole ethical  and moral dilemma as well  google and facebook are notorious for  privacy concerns now none of this is to  say that you shouldn't pursue a job at  feng feng is an outstanding place to  build your career and achieve financial  freedom but what feng isn't is a place  to achieve a long-term zen and that's  why turnover at feng is so high would  you leave a job at feng comment that  down below  also drop a like if you wish you had a  fake salary and of course consider  checking out our discord community to  suggest future video ideas and consider  subscribing see more questions logically  answered but until then i'm hari and  i'll see you guys on the next one  you
 

